tart":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"jv2s8TiODV"}],"key":"BOi9mLE4Zu"}],"urlSource":"blog.md","dataUrl":"/blog.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"jEAwg2YrlG"}],"key":"t5vywsN3b6"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recent blog posts","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"mYOu6Qaeei"}],"identifier":"recent-blog-posts","label":"Recent blog posts","html_id":"recent-blog-posts","implicit":true,"key":"wn05KAZAAT"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"My system for beating jet lag","key":"Pu9rfL8EQy"}],"key":"cNJCtJvnP6"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"NTwEJBHLfW"}],"key":"hW2D3gKUZO"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"aeveJ0ZZhP"}],"key":"sSmmGiLbY9"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"qEgRtuLsJI"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"mD1HQyUCUt"}],"key":"WS7cpetdSM"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"rYxb5HhFus"}],"key":"PYzOjkQU9M"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","key":"PGPqpMYplw"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"OActfBjilU"}],"key":"WaKmBt6Eeg"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"KObFkDWSWW"}],"key":"rNdN2VPz1J"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"CmP77TNVNi"}],"key":"XlQkoWQ2iZ"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"WJMRGNuHID"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"JaU59TYjtA"}],"key":"MneKUmOG7G"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"xFb6ykvFgl"}],"key":"X20MpQQOd4"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","key":"hJ0xmqG21u"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"TndlW2JD7Z"}],"key":"qpKnQet57U"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"LArIBxOgmZ"}],"key":"rImazBvJ90"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"ILGa7ajOFB"}],"key":"Rqq0GdFKij"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"YmqkA58EmI"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"JkmakdAOGw"}],"key":"yj5G03IHg1"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"iGgD0jF3DU"}],"key":"SCP1EEodA2"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","key":"aL3rEZlUSO"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"Rb0ofOW4ZC"}],"key":"TxHBrfkK33"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"SsQkgL5IyW"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"AJ61jYFD2i"}],"key":"AeEOGH4ssX"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"YKmSBGhUWD"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"QPtvvAybTQ"}],"key":"zLHw3jzhyG"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"vSMLphoUon"}],"key":"Cs5Ubq3Rzg"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"DyOrOqlDZK"}],"key":"zjdBI3kzFh"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"uLHqeAdAcr"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"CAsWmsZrDw"}],"key":"vs2QhODWa9"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"e5xQNJ6sPv"}],"key":"ZoIvpUbaya"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","key":"xolriSg1zo"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"aO5SzGHylO"}],"key":"VAMbVruJel"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"dy7kALVw8b"}],"key":"ovOLrHuSh6"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"GZW0rcviRd"}],"key":"SCwAwLLub1"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"Hn4C0ztTnh"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"WbCDaABlNj"}],"key":"Cm2L6S2Rhb"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"WbF7agZbpc"}],"key":"nFt5TmZ8ai"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","key":"e4WZzwsljj"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"g2cJuBmEOv"}],"key":"rwiX32NGO5"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"zBc9UZdyDR"}],"key":"eWzbjHuR82"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"WTgLSV14be"}],"key":"bYXwJXZaVN"},{"type":"text","value":"January 14, 2025 | ","key":"ZDf1E5cTvj"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"TuwP1kLIeJ"}],"key":"NSePhrF5BD"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"XajQUE4xX2"}],"key":"b1TtAnyaDV"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jec","key":"WafTVvkngq"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/bluesky","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How I'm trying to use BlueSky without getting burned again","key":"LLB279n4y2"}],"key":"stZ0jnwcUz"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some quick thoughts on moving from Twitter/X to BlueSky and how I'll try to use social media after being burned once by Twitter.\n","key":"ijEtJ2lzlc"}],"key":"PPXFffCmbn"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"KnPbNnKprj"}],"key":"xkCiL51soE"},{"type":"text","value":"November 22, 2024 | ","key":"CPeNsItpFM"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"y7mLG8q0EB"}],"key":"GE0HgRISru"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"WAgxUMs0wg"}],"key":"dLFNoMz7S2"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/bluesky","key":"wzNZHEaVzL"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/blog-list","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better blog lists with the MyST AST","key":"I334FBCMPs"}],"key":"z537RsmEgx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nOn my journey to learn more about writing with [the new MyST engine](https:///mystmd.org), I built upon [my recent update to my blog infrastructure](./programmatic-myst-with-jupyter.md) and made some improvements to my blog post list.\nHere's what it looks like now:\n\n````{note} Click here to see how it looks now\n:class: dropdown\n```{postlist}\n:number: 3\n```\n````\n\nHere's a quick rundown","key":"vdWi9e1fBZ"}],"key":"cXc8e5aMBb"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"b9Akw0Z8r8"}],"key":"EakdTMAlT6"},{"type":"text","value":"November 09, 2024 | ","key":"C0iy53j1Fd"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"b32mE27fde"}],"key":"chffhlhtFX"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"uJXKHHIu7I"}],"key":"Msk6Cil46O"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/blog-list","key":"reEQzqMlL3"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/programmatic-myst-with-jupyter","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate MyST with Jupyter and insert it into content programmatically","key":"xVOivXsWoi"}],"key":"Hmx7TaM91G"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\n\nWhile I've been [converting my blog to use the new MyST engine](./mystmd-with-the-blog.md), I discovered a useful MyST feature. It's not yet possible to [natively parse Jupyter Markdown outputs as MyST](https://github.com/jupyter-book/mystmd/issues/1026) but there's a workaround if you don't mind generating a temporary file.\n\nThe trick is to _write to a temporary file_","key":"AdjRVOzeLZ"}],"key":"UBXJ7vTC5J"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"Rdvfjn5c7D"}],"key":"cYyNumfyyL"},{"type":"text","value":"November 04, 2024 | ","key":"kF65Hi7qoO"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"cby2sgRDqK"}],"key":"XgMdtybD9q"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"kdf6SE8i7c"}],"key":"KjjxkQBF4x"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/programmatic-myst-with-jupyter","key":"AHRBrlGVgn"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/mystmd-with-the-blog","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-building my blog with MySTMD","key":"VSPlOXWoac"}],"key":"hu1UX8hvZ0"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nWow it has been a long time since I've last-written here. It turns out that having two small children and a very demanding job means you don't have as much time for blogging. But that's a whole different blog post...\n\nI've decided to convert my blog to use the new [MyST","key":"NuNV1u1ra2"}],"key":"VuS8jBb0qm"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"BaNhhYk8rA"}],"key":"zB4MdvOih5"},{"type":"text","value":"November 01, 2024 | ","key":"dUG5Ho1nwW"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"vgg9ogkw1S"}],"key":"zkTLciIGah"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"RG1HFh4zOA"}],"key":"AOh3plR1KS"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/mystmd-with-the-blog","key":"PtTNqm2M6u"}],"key":"vVt4lz8tHA"}],"key":"SQlpa7wVmt"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"next":{"title":"About me","url":"/about","group":"Welcome"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}